  "assessment": "The source provides the statistical mean-field effective detuning diagnostic delta_eff = delta - (4-2*d_H)/4 * sqrt(delta^2 + gamma^2/4) in the main text (lines 573-575) and End Matter (lines 707-710), with the interface energy scale eta(delta) = (1/4)*sqrt(delta^2 + gamma^2/4) (lines 697-699). The routing hint specifies public controls delta in [1,3] and d_H in [1,2], and private branches c=1 (statistical-interface correction) and c=0 (homogeneous single-mode baseline). The source supports the formula with c=1 (the (4-2*d_H) factor) and the homogeneous baseline c=0 corresponds to the single-mode mean-field with no interface correction (delta_eff = delta). The source does not explicitly state the domain delta in [1,3] and d_H in [1,2] for this diagnostic; the hint provides these as the intended public controls. The source states the diagnostic is a necessary-condition lower bound for the critical detuning, not the true numerical critical point. The extraction includes one mechanism with the effective detuning equation, two controls (delta, d_H), one readout (delta_eff), and two claims for the two branches. The case is authoring-ready because the source supports a numeric control-to-readout relation with explicit parameters.",
